    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='data'>
      <repository-location id='data' path='/workbooks/HealthFacilities_17297773475650' revision='' />
      <style />
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98002' id='11' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='48116' x='51345' y='999'>
            <zone h='98002' id='25' is-fixed='true' type-v2='layout-basic' w='48116' x='51345' y='999'>
              <zone h='17101' id='10' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='48116' x='51345' y='999'>
                <zone h='17101' id='24' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='48116' x='51345' y='999' />
              </zone>
              <zone h='80901' id='26' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='48116' x='51345' y='18100'>
                <zone fixed-size='585' forceUpdate='true' h='74033' id='12' is-fixed='true' type-v2='text' w='48116' x='51345' y='18100'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>The purpose of this analysis is to come up with health care solutions for the County of Nairobi that align with the Sustainable Development Goal (SDG3) for Universal Health.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>The data used for the analysis is population data from </run>
                    <run auto-url='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://africaopendata.org/dataset/2019-kenya-population-and-housing-census&amp;quot;'>https://africaopendata.org/dataset/2019-kenya-population-and-housing-census</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'> and the health facilities data from:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run auto-url='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://africaopendata.org/dataset/health-facilities-in-kenya&amp;quot;'>https://africaopendata.org/dataset/health-facilities-in-kenya</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>District Hospitals are secondary-level healthcare facilities serving a specific population within a district. According to WHO, they should offer a wide range of services, including family medicine, primary care, pediatrics, and eye care. They typically provide 24-hour care and serve as key healthcare providers in the community.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Health care centers are smaller and more localized. They should provide essential services including primary health care for common illnesses and minor injuries,maternal and child health services such as prenatal care and postnatal support.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Medical clinics often provide outpatient care and specialize in  treatment for non-emergency conditions.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Nursing Homes focus on long-term care for the elderly or people with chronic illnesses. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='11'>Maternity homes specialize in maternal and neonatal care. They focus on childbirth, prenatal, and postnatal care.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='13549' id='19' is-centered='0' is-scaled='1' param='Image/Screenshot 2025-06-16 161919.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='50806' x='539' y='999'>
